# How has this been tested?
Ran both a C96C48_hybatmDA test and a C768C384 test.  Both resulted in bitwise identical results in all EUPD outputs and product files.

The C76C384 test case included all 80 ensemble members and was executed from 2021122100 through 2021122400.  All product files were identical.  However, the netCDF analysis files differed, though the data sections were identical.  The exact location of the difference could not be found via ncdump and appears to be outside of the data and metadata sections.  The differences lie within the dimension section of a few variables, for instance `snmr` (snow mixing ratio).  The hex dump showed all 0s in the develop branch and all Fs in the test branch.  I don't believe that these differences are significant and I believe they may suggest a reproducibility issue in the GSI (or possibly GSI Utils), not the EnKF.  I have copied two such files to `/lfs/h2/emc/global/noscrub/david.huber/keep/diff_anl/{test,baseline}/gdas.20211224/00/analysis/atmos/gdas.t00z.atmanl.nc`.

The tests showed a slight speedup in runtimes of enkf.x, from an average of 1633s to 1603s with a standard deviation of 62.8s.  Below are the runtimes for each case:


